        '## Runtime Liveness at `v` 2 > ### Wire format': (
            ('Rules:'),
            ('Field order is exactly as shown:'),
            ('`boot_id`, `capability_hash`, `device_id`, `nonce`, `runtime_seq`, `v`, the '
             'lexicographic canonical order.'),
            ('`nonce` is a JSON string of exactly 32 characters, each one of `0`-`9` or '
             '`a`-`f`.'),
            ('A string of any other length, one containing an uppercase letter or any other '
             'character, `null`, and any other JSON type are `malformed`.'),
            ('`v` is `2`.'),
            ('`boot_id`, `capability_hash`, `device_id` and `runtime_seq`, the signature and '
             'its encoding, and the rule that any deviation is `malformed` and is refused '
             'before the signature is verified, are those of [Runtime Liveness](#wire-format), '
             'unchanged.'),
            ('A liveness object at `"v":1` has the grammar of [Wire format](#wire-format) '
             'exactly, and a `nonce` in it is an extra field and `malformed`.'),
            ('A `v` other than the integer `1` or `2` is `malformed`.'),
        ),
        '## Runtime Liveness at `v` 2 > ### Acceptance': (
            ('A device accepts a liveness message at either `v` only if it was not delivered '
             'retained, and then in the order of [Freshness without a device '
             'clock](#freshness-without-a-device-clock): it parses;'),
            ('`device_id` matches; the signature verifies against the provisioned runtime key;'),
            ("`boot_id` equals the device's current boot;"),
            ("`capability_hash` equals the device's accepted manifest hash; and `runtime_seq` "
             'strictly exceeds the last value accepted for this boot.'),
            ('One high-water mark serves both versions: a `v` `2` message whose `runtime_seq` '
             'does not exceed that of an accepted `v` `1` message is refused, and the reverse.'),
            ('A refused message changes nothing, including the held nonce below.'),
            ('Each check that fails names the refusal, with the same reason names the [`v` `1` '
             'liveness corpus](#golden-vectors) uses.'),
            ('The checks are made in this order, and a message that fails more than one is '
             'refused for the first that fails:'),
            ('| Order | Check | Reason |'),
            ('| 1 | it was not delivered retained | `retained` |'),
            ('| 2 | it parses under the grammar of its `v` | `malformed` |'),
            ('| 3 | `device_id` matches | `device_mismatch` |'),
            ('| 4 | the signature verifies | `signature_invalid` |'),
            ('| 5 | `boot_id` equals the current boot | `boot_mismatch` |'),
            ('| 6 | `capability_hash` equals the accepted manifest hash | '
             '`capability_hash_mismatch` |'),
            ('| 7 | `runtime_seq` exceeds the last accepted value | `seq_not_increasing` |'),
            ('Delivery is decided before content, so a retained delivery is refused as '
             '`retained` whatever its bytes.'),
            ('Checks 2 to 7 are those of [Runtime Liveness](#runtime-liveness), in its order, '
             'and apply to a `v` `1` message unchanged.'),
            ('A refusal carries no verdict back to the runtime.'),
        ),
        '## Runtime Liveness at `v` 2 > ### The held nonce': (
            ('A device holds at most one liveness nonce, in memory only, and never persists it.'),
            ('Holding none, which a reading envelope signs as `null`, means the device has no '
             'usable freshness reference.'),
            ('It does not mean that no runtime was watching.'),
            ("Accepting a `v` `2` message sets the held nonce to that message's `nonce`."),
            ('Accepting a `v` `1` message clears it.'),
            ('Every boot starts with none held.'),
            ("A change of the device's accepted manifest, or of its active runtime command key, "
             'clears it.'),
            ('The expiry of the liveness expiry window ([Timing](#timing)) clears it: once the '
             'device treats the runtime as unreachable, it holds no nonce until it accepts a '
             '`v` `2` message again.'),
            ('Clearing the held nonce, for any of these reasons, never alters a nonce already '
             'captured for a measurement in progress, or one already signed into an envelope, '
             'buffered or not.'),
            ('What the device does with the held nonce is defined in '
             '[firmware-telemetry/v2.md](../firmware-telemetry/v2.md#how-old-a-reading-is): it '
             'signs it into each reading envelope it measures afterwards.'),
        ),
        "## Runtime Liveness at `v` 2 > ### The runtime's nonce": (
            ('The runtime generates each `nonce` from a cryptographically secure random source, '
             '128 bits, fresh for every liveness message it signs.'),
            ('It never derives one from `runtime_seq`, from its state store, from a clock or '
             'from another message, and never reuses one, including for a message it signs '
             'again under a `runtime_seq` it has signed before.'),
            ('Before using a nonce, the runtime checks it against the nonces its live table '
             'holds (firmware-telemetry/v2, How Old A Reading Is), and generates another on a '
             'collision.'),
            ('The runtime records the nonce in that table under the signing-start rule of '
             '[firmware-telemetry/v2.md](../firmware-telemetry/v2.md#the-bound).'),
            ('The supervision window, the publication interval and every other obligation on '
             'publishing liveness in [Runtime Obligations](#runtime-obligations) apply to `v` '
             '`2` unchanged.'),
            ('**Why a nonce and not `runtime_seq`.** `runtime_seq` is persisted across runtime '
             'restarts, so restoring an older state store reissues a value the runtime has '
             'already signed.'),
            ('For the same boot and manifest, the reissued message is byte-identical to the '
             'earlier one, signature included.'),
            ('A bound keyed by `runtime_seq`, or by any digest of the message or its signature, '
             'would then date a reading taken under the first message by the time of the '
             'second.'),
            ('A fresh random nonce does not repeat across a restore.'),
            ('`runtime_seq` stays because the device still needs it to refuse replays without '
             'persisting anything, and the nonce gives no order.'),
        ),
        '## Runtime Liveness at `v` 2 > ### Which `v` the runtime publishes': (
            ('The runtime publishes one liveness message to each supervised device in every '
             'publication interval, at `v` `2`, and never publishes liveness at `v` `1`.'),
            ('**The declaration is the signal.** A device whose accepted manifest declares '
             '`runtime_key_domains` '
             '([firmware-telemetry/v2.md](../firmware-telemetry/v2.md#runtime-key-domains)) '
             'accepts liveness at `v` `2`.'),
            ('A device whose manifest does not declare it is sent no liveness message at either '
             '`v`, under [Signing Domains](#signing-domains).'),
            ('So every device the runtime may supervise has told it, in signed configuration its '
             'provisioning approval accepted, that it accepts `v` `2`.'),
            ('**No inferred support.** The runtime MUST NOT infer that a device accepts `v` `2` '
             'from a timeout, from the absence of a refusal, or from anything else its liveness '
             'traffic shows.'),
            ('A refused liveness message carries no verdict back, so silence proves nothing.'),
            ('The declaration is the only signal.'),
            ("**No substitute at `v` `1`.** A failure to generate, sign or publish an interval's "
             'message leaves that interval with no message.'),
            ('The runtime MUST NOT send a `v` `1` message in its place.'),
            ('This gives up a second, independent chance per interval to refresh supervision: a '
             '`v` `1` message published beside the `v` `2` one could survive a failed nonce draw, '
             'a transient signing or publish failure of the `v` `2` message, or the loss of that '
             'message in delivery.'),
            ('That cost is accepted.'),
            ('The expiry window is sized for one message per interval and tolerates isolated loss '
             '([Timing](#timing)); a failure that outlasts it is one the device should learn of '
             'by silence, not have masked by a message that clears its held nonce.'),
            ('A clock the runtime cannot read costs only the table entry, under the no-clock rule '
             'of [firmware-telemetry/v2.md](../firmware-telemetry/v2.md#the-bound), and the '
             'message is still published.'),
            ('What a failed signing leaves in the liveness table is the signing-start rule of '
             '[firmware-telemetry/v2.md](../firmware-telemetry/v2.md#the-bound).'),
            ('A runtime that cannot publish for longer than the expiry window leaves the device '
             'treating it as unreachable, and orphaned if no gateway is reachable either.'),
            ('**Conservative delivery.** When a message is lost, the device holds the nonce of '
             'the last message it accepted, or none.'),
            ('When messages arrive out of order, a late one is refused as `seq_not_increasing` '
             'and changes nothing.'),
            ('Lost or reordered messages may leave a reading with no bound, and never give a '
             'tighter bound than the truth.'),
            ('**Liveness never takes command capacity.** A device that reconnects on a persistent '
             'session can receive several queued liveness messages at once, beside its queued '
             'commands and its retained provisioning approval.'),
            ('A device governed by this contract MUST NOT let liveness messages, however many '
             'arrive together, take inbound capacity that a command or provisioning message would '
             'otherwise have, for example by giving liveness a separate inbound lane, or by '
             'reserving depth for commands and provisioning that liveness cannot use.'),
            ('It may drop liveness messages instead.'),
            ('A dropped liveness message loses a bound or a refresh of supervision.'),
            ('Liveness dropped for longer than the expiry window leaves the device treating the '
             'runtime as unreachable, with the consequences [Runtime '
             'Liveness](#expiry-and-what-a-device-does-before-it-hears-anything) gives, which with'
             ' no reachable gateway include orphaning.'),
            ('That is the intended direction of failure: toward local protection, never toward a '
             'stale claim of supervision.'),
            ('A device SHOULD also keep inbound capacity for liveness that commands and '
             'provisioning cannot take, so that command load, including a flood of commands it '
             'refuses, cannot by itself starve supervision.'),
            ('This version does not require a clean session.'),
            ('**Authority is unchanged.** Supervision comes from accepted liveness at either `v`, '
             'exactly as at `v` `1`, and nothing about what licenses an action changes.'),
            ('Whether the device holds a nonce governs age evidence only, never supervision or '
             'authority.'),
            ('A device still accepts liveness at `v` `1` under [Acceptance](#acceptance), with '
             'one high-water mark across both versions.'),
            ('A runtime that adopted this version before this section signs `v` `1` messages in '
             'the liveness domain, and a device that carries `runtime_key_domains` accepts them '
             'and clears its held nonce.'),
            ('**Why no rollout pair and no fleet-wide cut-over.** A device that carries '
             '`runtime_key_domains` accepts `v` `2`, and a device that does not is sent no '
             'liveness message, so this version admits no device that accepts only `v` `1` and '
             'could be supervised.'),
            ('Publishing `v` `1` beside `v` `2` would supervise no one, would clear the held '
             'nonce between the two messages, and would double the liveness traffic a constrained '
             "device's inbound lane takes."),
            ('A fleet-wide cut-over would decide by date what the manifest already states per '
             'device.'),
            ('**Limits.** A device whose manifest carries `runtime_key_domains` but whose '
             'verifier accepts only `v` `1` misstates its capability.'),
            ('It refuses every message as `malformed`, reports the runtime unreachable once its '
             'expiry window lapses, and orphans when no gateway is reachable.'),
            ('The runtime cannot detect this, and this version owes such a device nothing more: '
             'its own signed manifest is wrong, and it fails as lost supervision does.'),
            ('The producer test of '
             '[firmware-telemetry/v2.md](../firmware-telemetry/v2.md#required-implementation-artifacts) '
             "checks that a device's declaration and its verifier agree."),
