# --- status-record notes ---------------------------------------------------------
#
# Every note in status/firmware-commands/v2.json, the top-level one and each adoption
# entry's, held verbatim: a note states what implements this contract and what
# proof exists, and the status checker reads neither. A note added, removed or
# changed fails here until this table is updated in review.
STATUS_NOTES: tuple[tuple[str, str], ...] = (
    ('notes',
     'Exists for the rate_limited verdict, which answers relay_close only, and for the '
     'rule that a runtime never reissues a command to recover its delivery. Fresh '
     'open_protected_circuit attempts for a latched Tier D trip are not reissues and '
     'continue, under the binding the governing safety-profile contract authorizes. '
     "Command and provisioning approval bytes are v1's and keep v 1. Runtime liveness "
     "at v 1 keeps the grammar of this version's Runtime Liveness section and gains v "
     '2, carrying a fresh 128-bit nonce from which the signing runtime bounds how long '
     'ago a device began the transaction behind a reading, under firmware-telemetry/v2. '
     'A device that declares runtime_key_domains accepts liveness at v 2, and the '
     'runtime publishes liveness to it at v 2 alone, never at v 1. The edge firmware '
     'accepts liveness at v 2 and carries runtime_key_domains; the runtime implements '
     'the nonce and the liveness table, but publishes v 2 only behind a flag that is '
     'off by default. That is implementation, not end-to-end or HIL proof, and no '
     'device image gates a Local Interlock on liveness. The runtime has adopted the '
     'rate_limited and no-reissue rules; the edge firmware signs the rate_limited '
     'verdict from a3c54c2. The runtime adopts it before any device signs a v 2 fault, '
     'and devices accept liveness v 2 before the runtime publishes it. The runtime '
